    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d538">

                <pb facs="0881" n="865" sameAs="frus:frus1951v07p1/pg865"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">795.00/8–3051</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum of Conversation, by the Director of the
                        Office of Northeast Asian Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1951-08-30">August 30, 1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Subject: Political Steps in Event of Armistice in Korea.</p>
                <p>
                    <table>
                        <row>
                            <cell>Participants:</cell>
                            <cell>Mr. F.S. Tomlinson, Counselor, British Embassy</cell>
                        </row>
                        <row>
                            <cell/>
                            <cell>Mr. U. Alexis Johnson, Director, NA
                            </cell>
                        </row>
                    </table>
                </p>
                <p>I today handed to Mr. Tomlinson the attached memorandum in reply to the
                    memorandum of August 6 left with the Department by the British Embassy.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d538-f1"/> I told Mr. Tomlinson that this was an informal and
                    unofficial memorandum comparable to the communication we had received from
                    them.</p>



                <xi:include href="d538-a1.xml" xpointer="d538-a1"/>
